{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-19143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨2,1,-1⟩$ and $b=⟨1,4,2⟩.$ Find ${\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a-{\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974503/state.json" "file_sha256" "86a893c7d09712a9d5acc21490a552b177b944887b350e0183ed6fc0788cd0a1"} {"question" "q-19143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{21}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b & =\\frac{b\\cdot a}{|\\,a\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{6}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a-{\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{21}}-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{6}-4\\sqrt{21}}{\\sqrt{126}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974503/state.json" "file_sha256" "86a893c7d09712a9d5acc21490a552b177b944887b350e0183ed6fc0788cd0a1"} {"question" "q-19143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974503/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c32cb234cb19882c767eb9c557904457a5ade56ca1841f4fed40f02eb224bc3d"} {"question" "q-19143" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974503/state.json" "file_sha256" "86a893c7d09712a9d5acc21490a552b177b944887b350e0183ed6fc0788cd0a1"} {"question" "q-19143" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "\\frac{4\\sqrt{6}-4\\sqrt{21}}{\\sqrt{126}}"] ["math" "\\frac{4\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{21}}{\\sqrt{126}}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}-4\\sqrt{21}}{\\sqrt{126}}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{21}}{\\sqrt{126}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974503/state.json" "file_sha256" "86a893c7d09712a9d5acc21490a552b177b944887b350e0183ed6fc0788cd0a1"} {"question" "q-19143" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4\\sqrt{6}-4\\sqrt{21}}{\\sqrt{126}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974503/state.json" "file_sha256" "86a893c7d09712a9d5acc21490a552b177b944887b350e0183ed6fc0788cd0a1"} {"question" "q-237022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $p=⟨3,5,x⟩$ and $q=⟨-3,1,2⟩.$ Given that the scalar projection of $p$ onto $q$ is zero, find the value of $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974503/state.json" "file_sha256" "86a893c7d09712a9d5acc21490a552b177b944887b350e0183ed6fc0788cd0a1"} {"question" "q-237022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $p$ is a nonzero vector, its scalar projection onto another nonzero vector $q$ equals zero only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\np⊥q\\,⟹\\,p\\cdot q=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & ={p}_{x}\\cdot {q}_{x}+{p}_{y}\\cdot {q}_{y}+{p}_{z}\\cdot {q}_{z} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-3)+5\\cdot 1+x\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2x-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =0 \\\\ 2x-4 & =0 \\\\ 2x & =4 \\\\ x & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974503/state.json" "file_sha256" "86a893c7d09712a9d5acc21490a552b177b944887b350e0183ed6fc0788cd0a1"} {"question" "q-237022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974503/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c32cb234cb19882c767eb9c557904457a5ade56ca1841f4fed40f02eb224bc3d"} {"question" "q-237022" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974503/state.json" "file_sha256" "86a893c7d09712a9d5acc21490a552b177b944887b350e0183ed6fc0788cd0a1"} {"question" "q-237022" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974503/state.json" "file_sha256" "86a893c7d09712a9d5acc21490a552b177b944887b350e0183ed6fc0788cd0a1"} {"question" "q-237022" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974503/state.json" "file_sha256" "86a893c7d09712a9d5acc21490a552b177b944887b350e0183ed6fc0788cd0a1"} {"question" "q-275253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $p=⟨-1,2,1⟩$ and $q=⟨2,x,0⟩.$ Given that the scalar projection of $p$ onto $q$ is zero, find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974503/state.json" "file_sha256" "86a893c7d09712a9d5acc21490a552b177b944887b350e0183ed6fc0788cd0a1"} {"question" "q-275253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $p$ is a nonzero vector, its scalar projection onto another nonzero vector $q$ equals zero only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\np⊥q\\,⟹\\,p\\cdot q=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & ={p}_{x}\\cdot {q}_{x}+{p}_{y}\\cdot {q}_{y}+{p}_{z}\\cdot {q}_{z} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 2+2\\cdot x+1\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =-2+2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =0 \\\\ -2+2x & =0 \\\\ 2x & =2 \\\\ x & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974503/state.json" "file_sha256" "86a893c7d09712a9d5acc21490a552b177b944887b350e0183ed6fc0788cd0a1"} {"question" "q-275253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974503/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c32cb234cb19882c767eb9c557904457a5ade56ca1841f4fed40f02eb224bc3d"} {"question" "q-275253" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974503/state.json" "file_sha256" "86a893c7d09712a9d5acc21490a552b177b944887b350e0183ed6fc0788cd0a1"} {"question" "q-275253" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974503/state.json" "file_sha256" "86a893c7d09712a9d5acc21490a552b177b944887b350e0183ed6fc0788cd0a1"} {"question" "q-318977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $p=⟨4,-1,1⟩$ and $q=⟨1,2,2⟩.$ Find the scalar projection of $p$ onto $q.$\n\n${\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974503/state.json" "file_sha256" "86a893c7d09712a9d5acc21490a552b177b944887b350e0183ed6fc0788cd0a1"} {"question" "q-318977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the scalar projection formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p & =\\frac{p\\cdot q}{|\\,q\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{p}_{x}{q}_{x}+{p}_{y}{q}_{y}+{p}_{z}{q}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{q}_{x}^{2}+{q}_{y}^{2}+{q}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(4)(1)+(-1)(2)+(1)(2)}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-2+2}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974503/state.json" "file_sha256" "86a893c7d09712a9d5acc21490a552b177b944887b350e0183ed6fc0788cd0a1"} {"question" "q-318977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974503/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c32cb234cb19882c767eb9c557904457a5ade56ca1841f4fed40f02eb224bc3d"} {"question" "q-318977" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974503/state.json" "file_sha256" "86a893c7d09712a9d5acc21490a552b177b944887b350e0183ed6fc0788cd0a1"} {"question" "q-318977" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974503/state.json" "file_sha256" "86a893c7d09712a9d5acc21490a552b177b944887b350e0183ed6fc0788cd0a1"} {"question" "q-319171" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $p=⟨4,1,-2⟩$ and $q=⟨1,x,3⟩.$ Given that the scalar projection of $p$ onto $q$ is zero, find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974503/state.json" "file_sha256" "86a893c7d09712a9d5acc21490a552b177b944887b350e0183ed6fc0788cd0a1"} {"question" "q-319171" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $p$ is a nonzero vector, its scalar projection onto another nonzero vector $q$ equals zero only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\np⊥q\\,⟹\\,p\\cdot q=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & ={p}_{x}\\cdot {q}_{x}+{p}_{y}\\cdot {q}_{y}+{p}_{z}\\cdot {q}_{z} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1+1\\cdot x+(-2)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =x-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =0 \\\\ x-2 & =0 \\\\ x & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974503/state.json" "file_sha256" "86a893c7d09712a9d5acc21490a552b177b944887b350e0183ed6fc0788cd0a1"} {"question" "q-319171" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974503/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c32cb234cb19882c767eb9c557904457a5ade56ca1841f4fed40f02eb224bc3d"} {"question" "q-319171" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974503/state.json" "file_sha256" "86a893c7d09712a9d5acc21490a552b177b944887b350e0183ed6fc0788cd0a1"} {"question" "q-319171" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answ